    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/research-engineer-cyclone-testing-station-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Research Engineer, Cyclone Testing Station",
      "description": "Research Engineer, Cyclone Testing Station - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Research Engineer, Cyclone Testing Station 495897 Townsville Academic Full time Closing on: Oct 18 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Academic Level B | Full-time (1.0 FTE) | Continuing appointment] | Townsville Help improve the resilience of Australian buildings and communities to severe weather Deliver applied engineering research with meaningful industry and community impact Join the internationally relevant work of JCU’s Cyclone Testing Station Level B $112,810 - $133,110 + 17% Super & great benefits James Cook University is seeking a collaborative and solutions-focused Research Engineer to join the Cyclone Testing Station in Townsville. This is an exciting opportunity to apply your engineering expertise to research that helps reduce the social and financial impacts of tropical cyclones, thunderstorms and other severe wind events. You will contribute to practical projects examining building performance, wind loads, wind-driven debris and rain damage, while working with industry, researchers and technical specialists to strengthen community resilience. About the role As a Research Engineer, you will utilise your engineering expertise to engage with existing and prospective clients, develop suitable testing programs, supervise load testing activities and guide technical staff to ensure engineering best practice is achieved. Working within the Cyclone Testing Station, you will contribute to research and testing that helps communities minimise the loss and suffering caused by cyclones and other high wind events. You will conduct and oversee testing programs, analyse data, prepare technical reports and research publications, and communicate outcomes through industry engagement, workshops and conferences. You will also collaborate with industry partners, contribute to research informing Australian Standards, and support activities including grant applications, damage investigations and community engagement initiatives that strengthen the resilience of buildings and communities across Australia Key responsibilities In this role, you will: Design and deliver testing programs aligned with relevant standards and engineering design criteria Apply structural analysis, laboratory testing, field investigation and probability analysis techniques Analyse and interpret data, preparing clear technical reports and research publications Collaborate with technical staff and multidisciplinary colleagues to deliver high-quality testing outcomes Build effective relationships with clients, industry organisations and project stakeholders Monitor project progress and communicate outcomes against agreed milestones Contribute to research supporting building resilience and relevant Australian Standards Support the Cyclone Testing Station’s damage investigations, grant activities and community engagement initiatives About you You will bring qualifications and experience in wind, structural or mechanical engineering, or a related discipline, appropriate to appointment at Academic Level B. You will also demonstrate: Contemporary knowledge of Australian Building Standards, relevant legislation and building construction techniques Experience delivering research projects, analysing data and communicating findings through reports or journal publications Strong engineering analysis, problem-solving and organisational capabilities The ability to manage priorities, exercise sound judgement and meet competing deadlines Experience engaging with industry and translating research into practical outcomes Excellent written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills The ability to work effectively both independently and within a multidisciplinary research team Familiarity with building systems and construction techniques, together with experience using numerical or structural analysis software, will be highly regarded. About the Cyclone Testing Station The Cyclone Testing Station (CTS) is a leading research and consulting centre within James Cook University's College of Science and Engineering. CTS delivers world-class research, testing and consulting services focused on improving the resilience of buildings and communities to cyclones, thunderstorms and other severe wind events. Through collaboration with industry, government and Standards Australia, our work helps reduce the social and economic impacts of natural disasters and create safer, more resilient communities. ] Learn more about CTS on the Cyclone Testing Station website . Why work at JCU? Join Australia’s university for the Tropics and contribute to applied engineering research that supports safer, stronger and more resilient communities. At JCU, you will enjoy: 5 weeks annual leave plus leave loading Flexible work arrangements Up to 12 months paid parental leave Salary packaging options Paid study leave and staff development programs Fitness Passport and health insurance discounts Free Employee Assistance Program, including coaching and counselling How to apply Click the Apply button or apply through the JCU Careers page and: Complete the online application form Upload your current resume Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience against the key requirements and how your skills will contribute to your success in the role For further information, please contact David Henderson on (07) 4781 6364 or email david.henderson@jcu.edu.au JCU celebrates diversity and is committed to creating a safe, inclusive and welcoming environment. We encourage applications from people of all backgrounds who meet the requirements of the role. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) a2c9944e Last Name (required) ee9824b8 Email (required) 6568befd Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Space Systems Coordinator Townsville Professional Coordinate accurate space systems, data and stakeholder services that support effective University space planning, utilisation and minor works decisions. Manager, Space and Minor Works Projects Townsville Professional Lead the strategic planning and delivery of space, workplace design and minor works projects that enhance JCU’s built environment and support safe, sustainable and effective outcomes. Student Scholarship and Loans Officer Townsville Professional Support student success through the administration of scholarships, bursaries, and financial assistance programs while delivering outstanding service and advice to students and stakeholders. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) c5d13fa4 Last Name (required) f098ff04 Email (required) 472a33cf Job Alert f50b3a33 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Science & Engineering College of Science & Engineering Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/communications-and-engagement-officer-townsville-qld-australia-91f827ca-58a2-4ae6-bb83-1ce681ca40b2": {
      "title": "Communications and Engagement Officer",
      "description": "Communications and Engagement Officer - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Communications and Engagement Officer 495609 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Oct 18 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Passionate about communications, content and creating positive student experiences? Join JCU in this fixed-term role to February 2028, as a Communications and Engagement Officer , supporting digital communications, student engagement activities and events that help our student community feel informed, connected and supported. This is a great opportunity for a recent graduate or early-career professional looking to build practical experience across communications, content creation and event delivery within a supportive team. Full-time, Fixed Term to February 2028 | 36.25hrs per week Based on-site at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, Douglas HEWL 5: $78,740.56 - $89,310.33 per annum plus up to 17% employer superannuation contributions, leave loading and other generous employee benefits. ABOUT THE ROLE In this role, you’ll help create a positive and engaging experience for JCU students through communications, digital content and events. You’ll create and share content across a variety of channels, supporting students to stay informed, connected and engaged throughout their time at university. Working alongside experienced colleagues, you’ll support the planning and delivery of student events and engagement activities, helping ensure they run smoothly and provide a positive experience for students. You’ll have opportunities to develop your skills, contribute ideas and build experience across different areas of communications and engagement. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE We’re looking for someone at the beginning of, or looking to build, their career in communications, marketing or events. You’ll have qualifications in Marketing, Communications, Journalism, Events or a related field, or an equivalent combination of relevant skills, experience and training. You may have developed your experience through employment, study, placements, internships, volunteering or community involvement. You’ll be able to create clear and engaging content, communicate confidently with different people and use Microsoft Office and digital communication tools. You do not need to have worked in every system listed, but you should be comfortable learning new technology. You’ll be organised, attentive to detail and comfortable managing different priorities with support from your team. Experience assisting with events, photography, videography or content creation will be well regarded but is not essential. If you’re a proactive and creative communicator who enjoys working with others and is keen to develop your skills while contributing to the student experience, we’d love to hear from you. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville campus HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Caitlin Dobson via email at caitlin.dobson1@jcu.edu.au . ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) eb442396 Last Name (required) 71743205 Email (required) 36a2a890 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Space Systems Coordinator Townsville Professional Coordinate accurate space systems, data and stakeholder services that support effective University space planning, utilisation and minor works decisions. Manager, Space and Minor Works Projects Townsville Professional Lead the strategic planning and delivery of space, workplace design and minor works projects that enhance JCU’s built environment and support safe, sustainable and effective outcomes. Student Scholarship and Loans Officer Townsville Professional Support student success through the administration of scholarships, bursaries, and financial assistance programs while delivering outstanding service and advice to students and stakeholders. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) ef37533d Last Name (required) 48085131 Email (required) f40f41ab Job Alert dce3b2b3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Student Services & Support Student Services & Support Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
