    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/prospect-intelligence-analyst-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Prospect Intelligence Analyst",
      "description": "Prospect Intelligence Analyst - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Prospect Intelligence Analyst 495915 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Oct 27 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Join JCU as a Prospect Intelligence Analyst and use research, data and emerging technologies to help shape philanthropic opportunities. Working across prospect identification, due diligence, portfolio analysis and reporting, you’ll provide the intelligence needed to support fundraising priorities and strengthen engagement with prospective donors. Full-time, continuing opportunity | 36.25 hours per week Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, Douglas HEWL 6: $90,821 - $98,369 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation Flexible working arrangements may be considered for the successful candidate who brings direct prospect research experience ABOUT THE ROLE As the Prospect Intelligence Analyst , you will deliver high-quality research, intelligence profiles and briefing materials that provide clear and timely insights for philanthropic fundraising and engagement. You will support prospect management through portfolio analysis, tracking, pipeline reporting and due diligence, helping the Advancement team identify opportunities and make informed decisions. Working with Raiser’s Edge NXT and associated systems, you will maintain accurate and confidential prospect information while producing reports, dashboards and analytical insights that support fundraising planning and campaign readiness. You will also apply research methodologies, wealth screening tools and emerging technologies to strengthen prospect development activities. Through continuous improvement and collaboration across JCU, you will help refine Advancement systems, workflows and practices while providing specialist support that contributes to the University’s fundraising and engagement objectives. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You are a curious and analytical professional who enjoys uncovering insights from information and data. You can confidently research, assess and interpret information from multiple sources, turning your findings into clear recommendations, reports and briefings that support informed decision-making. With experience using databases, CRM systems and reporting tools, you understand the importance of data integrity, confidentiality and attention to detail. You thrive in a collaborative environment, manage competing priorities effectively and bring a proactive approach to identifying opportunities that support meaningful stakeholder engagement and organisational outcomes. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville campus HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload