      "title": "Casual HDR Program Support Officer",
      "description": "Casual HDR Program Support Officer - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Casual HDR Program Support Officer 495720 Townsville Professional Casual Closing on: Oct 26 2026 Graduate Research School (Townsville) $52.04 - $59.02 per hour We’re seeking a motivated casual HDR Program Support Officer to assist with candidature administration, milestone tracking and high‑quality support for HDR candidates and supervisors. You’ll help manage key processes across admissions, enrolments, variations, examinations and completions, while providing responsive customer service and accurate record‑keeping This role suits someone with strong organisational skills, attention to detail, confidence using enterprise systems, and the ability to work both independently and as part of a busy team. This position is based in Townsville and requires on-campus attendance. Current JCU students are not eligible to apply. How to Apply and Contact Details Apply now and help us create a healthier, more sustainable future for the Tropics. Click the ‘Apply’ button or visit the JCU Careers Page and follow these steps: Complete the application form Upload your current resume For further information, contact Gabby Ryan via email gabby.ryan@jcu.edu.au JCU celebrates diversity and is committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and welcoming environment for all. We encourage applications from people of all backgrounds who meet the role requirements. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) b758f552 Last Name (required) 5333c179 Email (required) a74ad186 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services (Clinical and Simulated Learning) Townsville Professional, Technical Lead safe, compliant and high-quality laboratory and technical services across Medicine, Nursing and Midwifery, Dentistry, Rehabilitation and Health Sciences, optimi