    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-senior-lecturer-environmental-hydrology-cairns-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Environmental Hydrology",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Environmental Hydrology - Cairns, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Environmental Hydrology 496038 Cairns Academic Full time Closing on: Nov 24 2026 Position Description Full-time 36.25 hours per week | Continuing Appointment Based in Cairns Academic Level B $112,810 - $133,110 | Academic Level C $137,166 - $157,465 17% Super, 5 weeks annual leave, leave loading plus other great benefits Build an internationally competitive research program addressing contemporary environmental challenges. Inspire the next generation of environmental scientists through practical, field-based learning. Collaborate with Traditional Owners, government, industry, communities and research partners. Advance understanding of tropical catchments, landscapes and land–water systems. James Cook University (JCU) is seeking an emerging or established academic with expertise in environmental hydrology to join our College of Science and Engineering in Cairns. This is an opportunity to shape teaching and research in catchment hydrology and soil–water–vegetation interactions while contributing to JCU’s established strengths in tropical land and water systems. Your work will connect scientific understanding with practical environmental management, particularly in northern Australia and tropical environments. About the role As a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Environmental Hydrology, you will deliver engaging undergraduate and postgraduate teaching while developing a high-quality, internationally competitive research program. You will contribute to teaching across Environmental Science and Management, Science and Environment programs, including lectures, practical classes, field-based learning and assessment. You will also supervise undergraduate, postgraduate and higher degree by research students, helping them develop the knowledge and practical capability to address complex environmental challenges. Your research will strengthen understanding of environmental and hydrological processes, with opportunities to explore areas such as catchment hydrology, soil–water–vegetation interactions, water resources management, agricultural practice, water quality and climate adaptation. Working across disciplines, you will build productive partnerships with Traditional Owners, government agencies, industry, community organisations, non-government organisations and research collaborators in Australia and internationally. Key responsibilities In this role, you will: Deliver and coordinate high-quality teaching in environmental hydrology, land and water science, and related disciplines. Develop an impactful research program in environmental science and hydrological processes. Pursue competitive research funding and contribute to multidisciplinary research initiatives. Establish collaborative teaching and research partnerships in northern Australia, nationally and internationally. Supervise undergraduate research, Honours, postgraduate and higher degree by research students. Engage with Traditional Owners, government, industry, community organisations and research partners. Strengthen JCU’s visibility and reputation through professional engagement and public outreach. Contribute positively to the academic and collegiate life of the College. About you You will hold, or be close to completing, a PhD in environmental hydrology, environmental science, earth science, physical geography or a related discipline, supported by expertise in catchment processes. You will bring: Research expertise in environmental science and hydrological processes, including catchment hydrology or soil–water–vegetation interactions. A record of high-quality research publications relative to your career stage and opportunities. The capability to develop an independent, competitive and collaborative research program. A commitment to delivering engaging, inclusive and high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate teaching. Experience or demonstrated potential in supervising undergraduate, postgraduate or higher degree by research students. The ability to plan and deliver research, teaching and field-based activities within multidisciplinary teams. The ability to communicate scientific information effectively to specialist and non-specialist audiences. A commitment to diversity, reconciliation and an inclusive working and learning environment. Experience in tropical or northern Australian environments, field-based teaching, quantitative analysis, spatial analysis or integrated catchment modelling will be highly regarded. We also welcome experience developing applied research partnerships or co-designing research with Traditional Owners, government, industry, non-government organisations or community groups. Why work at JCU? At JCU, your teaching and research can contribute directly to the environmental resilience and sustainable management of tropical landscapes and communities. Based in Cairns, you will work in a region that provides an exceptional setting for environmental teaching, field-based learning and applied research. You will join a collaborative academic community with opportunities to build interdisciplinary partnerships and connect your research with practical environmental challenges. JCU employees also enjoy a range of benefits, including: Five weeks’ annual leave plus leave loading. Flexible working arrangements. Up to 12 months’ paid parental leave. Salary packaging options. Paid study leave and staff development opportunities. Fitness Passport and health insurance discounts. A free Employee Assistance Program offering confidential coaching and counselling. Thinking of applying? We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples. We also welcome applications from candidates in the final stages of their PhD who are interested in structured mentoring pathways. If you do not meet every listed criterion, we still encourage you to apply and demonstrate your potential. JCU recognises that career pathways and opportunities differ. The selection panel will consider your achievements, potential and performance relative to the opportunities available to you. If you require assistance preparing your application or adjustments during the recruitment process, please let us know so we can support your participation. How to apply Click Apply and: Complete the online application form. Upload your current résumé. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience against the key requirements and how your skills will support your success in the role. Join JCU and use your expertise in environmental hydrology to inspire students, advance tropical research and help address some of the most important land and water challenges facing northern Australia and the Tropics. For further information please contact Professor Alana Grech on (07) 4781 4107 or via email alana.grech@jcu.edu.au Recommended for you Scheduling Services Officer Townsville Professional Bring your organizational, problem-solving and communication skills to a fast-paced environment, delivering accurate and efficient timetabling, class registration and scheduling services that support staff, students and the broader University community. Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services, AITHM Cairns Professional Join one of Australia's leading tropical research institutes and lead laboratory and technical services while overseeing the specialised research infrastructure that underpins globally significant health research. Influence strategy, build capability and drive excellence across a diverse and evolving research environment. Project Manager Townsville Professional Ready to lead and shape the future of our campus? Join JCU as a Project Manager and drive complex capital projects, from new builds and upgrades to major refurbishments. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/scheduling-services-officer-townsville-qld-australia-321e576f-08f6-40e8-b9d6-6f415d145c52": {
      "title": "Scheduling Services Officer",
      "description": "Scheduling Services Officer - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Scheduling Services Officer 496019 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Nov 8 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. We are seeking two organised and solutions-focused Scheduling Services Officers to join JCU on a fixed-term basis, bringing their scheduling, coordination and customer service expertise to deliver accurate, integrated timetable and class registration support across the University. One full-time, fixed-term opportunity until August 2027 | 36.25 hours per week One full-time, fixed-term opportunity until January 2028 | 36.25 hours per week Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, Douglas HEWL 5: $78,740 - $89,310 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE In this fast-paced and customer-focused role, you will contribute to the development, publication and ongoing maintenance of the University timetable, alongside student class registration and room booking services within a complex operating environment. Working as a partner to allocated academic areas, you will build strong stakeholder relationships, coordinate and prioritise competing scheduling requirements, and use specialist scheduling systems to deliver accurate, responsive and high-quality services that meet the needs of staff and students. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will bring demonstrated scheduling and coordination experience, including the effective allocation of resources and delivery of outcomes in a systematic and organised manner. You will have strong organisational, administrative, problem-solving and critical-thinking skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines. Highly developed communication and interpersonal skills will enable you to build effective stakeholder relationships, manage expectations, negotiate competing needs and navigate challenging situations. You will also have effective computer and data-entry skills, experience with Microsoft Office, and the ability to confidently learn and use specialist scheduling systems. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville and Cairns’ campuses HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Jenna Tolcher at jenna.tolcher@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information