    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/project-manager-townsville-qld-australia-2c25dca2-b270-4f44-94b1-3400ba23e764": {
      "title": "Project Manager",
      "description": "Project Manager - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Project Manager 496036 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Nov 1 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. An exciting opportunity is now available for an experienced Project Manager to join our Estate Directorate, leading the delivery of complex and high-impact capital works projects across the University. Full-time, continuing opportunity | 36.25 hours per week HEWL 9: $130,115 - $137,625 per annum, plus up to 17% employer superannuation contributions. Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, Douglas WHAT YOU CAN ACCOMPLISH IN THE ROLE Delivering capital projects in support of the University’s strategic plan, you will be responsible for the planning and implementation of complex building projects, extensions, refurbishments and infrastructure upgrades across campus and at off-site locations. Working closely with the Manager, Capital Projects, you will resolve project-related issues and provide day-to-day direction to consultants and contractors as required. You will play a key role in delivering capital works that enable JCU’s teaching, research and community objectives. Key responsibilities include: •              Planning and delivering complex building, refurbishment and infrastructure projects •              Managing projects across multiple campuses and off-site locations •              Providing day-to-day direction to consultants and contractors •              Partnering closely with the Estate team to resolve issues and maintain project momentum •              Ensuring projects are delivered on time, within budget and to specification WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE As an experienced Project Manager, you bring the expertise and professional judgement to lead the delivery of complex, high-value capital projects within a large and complex organisational environment. You are committed to achieving high-quality, best-practice outcomes while ensuring compliance with relevant legislation, regulations, codes and standards. You are a highly effective communicator and negotiator, experienced in building productive relationships and influencing a diverse range of internal and external stakeholders, including contractors, consultants and suppliers. With high-level judgement and problem-solving capability, you confidently navigate complex project challenges, competing priorities and significant time and resource requirements to deliver projects on time, within budget and to the required standards. You bring a strategic and solutions-focused approach, strong attention to detail and a genuine interest in sustainable building practices and emerging technologies. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave Flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville and Cairns’ campuses HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Nathan Shepherd at nathan.shepherd@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 8d2e34a9 Last Name (required) 9142ccf6 Email (required) bed916bd Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Environmental Hydrology Cairns Academic Advance solutions to some of the Tropics’ most pressing land and water challenges. Join James Cook University as a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Environmental Hydrology and build impactful research, inspire future environmental scientists, and collaborate with industry, government and community partners to create real-world environmental outcomes. Scheduling Services Officer Townsville Professional Bring your organizational, problem-solving and communication skills to a fast-paced environment, delivering accurate and efficient timetabling, class registration and scheduling services that support staff, students and the broader University community. Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services, AITHM Cairns Professional Join one of Australia's leading tropical research institutes and lead laboratory and technical services while overseeing the specialised research infrastructure that underpins globally significant health research. Influence strategy, build capability and drive excellence across a diverse and evolving research environment. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) d6303fcb Last Name (required) 2254f30a Email (required) b3740a8e Job Alert 39c0e133 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Estate Estate Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
