    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/strategic-asset-planner-townsville-qld-australia-5ef6ddae-8ae1-4aa7-915a-35cbd2cee864": {
      "title": "Strategic Asset Planner",
      "description": "Strategic Asset Planner - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Strategic Asset Planner 496020 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Nov 5 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Are you an ambitious and skilled Strategic Asset Planner ready for your next challenge? This is an exciting opportunity to lead JCU's asset planning, maintenance and replacement programs, influencing key investment decisions and driving asset performance, sustainability and compliance across a unique and diverse university estate. The position is full-time, on a continuing basis and based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, Douglas. HEWL 8: $111,960 - $128,567 per annum plus up to 17% employer superannuation contributions. ABOUT THE ROLE The Strategic Asset Planner leads the University's asset planning, maintenance and replacement programs in alignment with the Strategic Asset Management Framework and Estate Directorate maintenance strategy. The role delivers risk-informed asset planning and investment prioritisation that strengthens asset performance, sustainability and compliance outcomes across the University's built and natural environment. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will be a strategic and analytical asset management professional with experience delivering asset planning, maintenance and renewal programs within complex environments. You will bring qualifications and/or demonstrated experience in asset management, engineering, facilities management or a related discipline, together with a strong understanding of strategic asset management frameworks, lifecycle planning and risk-based investment decision-making. You will have the ability to develop and implement planned maintenance and asset replacement programs, using data, technical information and financial insights to inform practical and sustainable asset strategies. You will also bring strong leadership capability, with the ability to influence outcomes, build productive relationships and work effectively with technical, operational and corporate stakeholders. You will balance competing priorities and drive continuous improvement initiatives that enhance asset performance, service delivery and organisational outcomes. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave Flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville and Cairns’ campuses HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Daniel Nixon at daniel.nixon@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) fae4ee3d Last Name (required) 51831f53 Email (required) 918ba5e8 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Environmental Hydrology Cairns Academic Advance solutions to some of the Tropics’ most pressing land and water challenges. Join James Cook University as a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Environmental Hydrology and build impactful research, inspire future environmental scientists, and collaborate with industry, government and community partners to create real-world environmental outcomes. Scheduling Services Officer Townsville Professional Bring your organizational, problem-solving and communication skills to a fast-paced environment, delivering accurate and efficient timetabling, class registration and scheduling services that support staff, students and the broader University community. Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services, AITHM Cairns Professional Join one of Australia's leading tropical research institutes and lead laboratory and technical services while overseeing the specialised research infrastructure that underpins globally significant health research. Influence strategy, build capability and drive excellence across a diverse and evolving research environment. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) 78de6385 Last Name (required) c1c53883 Email (required) bc1229d8 Job Alert bbbac5b3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Estate Estate Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
