    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/institute-operations-manager-tmci-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Institute Operations Manager (TMCI)",
      "description": "Institute Operations Manager (TMCI) - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Institute Operations Manager (TMCI) 495927 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Nov 8 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Join one of Australia's leading tropical marine research universities and contribute to research that informs the sustainable management of marine and coastal environments. Use your operational and strategic experience to support the establishment of the new Tropical Marine and Coastal Institute and the delivery of world-class tropical marine and coastal research. You will provide strategic, financial and business expertise to establish its operations and governance, guide strategic projects, strengthen governance and risk management, and build productive relationships that support the Institute’s priorities and long-term sustainability. This is a fixed-term appointment for an initial 12 months, with the potential for a longer-term opportunity following the initial project. Full-time, fixed term for 12 months | 36.25 hours per week Based at JCU’s Bebegu Yumba campus in Townsville, gateway to the Great Barrier Reef and tropical North Queensland HEWL 8: $111,960 - $128,567 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE As Institute Operations Manager , you will help translate the Tropical Marine and Coastal Institute’s strategic priorities into practical and sustainable outcomes. Providing subject matter expertise and high-level project management, you will oversee key operational activities, contribute to budgeting and forecasting, and provide informed financial and business advice. Working closely with senior leaders and stakeholders, you will ensure operational priorities, projects and risks are clearly communicated and effectively managed. You will build productive internal and external relationships, support governance and compliance, and drive improvements to the processes and procedures that enable the Institute to deliver efficient, high-quality services. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will bring substantial experience in financial, business and strategic planning within a large or complex organisation, including the preparation of business cases, forecasts, plans and high-level reports. Your background will demonstrate an ability to develop and implement business strategies that support both operational delivery and longer-term organisational objectives. A confident communicator and collaborative relationship builder, you can work effectively with stakeholders at varying levels to achieve shared outcomes. You will also bring exceptional organisation, sound judgement and strong problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and develop practical solutions to complex issues. An understanding of marine and coastal research and the broader higher education and research environment will be highly regarded. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville campus HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Richard Cook at richard.cook1@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 51d04501 Last Name (required) 0a1c4e4f Email (required) 14612d92 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Environmental Hydrology Cairns Academic Advance solutions to some of the Tropics’ most pressing land and water challenges. Join James Cook University as a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Environmental Hydrology and build impactful research, inspire future environmental scientists, and collaborate with industry, government and community partners to create real-world environmental outcomes. Scheduling Services Officer Townsville Professional Bring your organizational, problem-solving and communication skills to a fast-paced environment, delivering accurate and efficient timetabling, class registration and scheduling services that support staff, students and the broader University community. Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services, AITHM Cairns Professional Join one of Australia's leading tropical research institutes and lead laboratory and technical services while overseeing the specialised research infrastructure that underpins globally significant health research. Influence strategy, build capability and drive excellence across a diverse and evolving research environment. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) d1605d47 Last Name (required) 617c9670 Email (required) 8912169e Job Alert 4204501a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Tropical Marine and Coastal Institute (TMCI) Tropical Marine and Coastal Institute (TMCI) Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
