    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-senior-lecturer-civil-engeering-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Civil Engeering",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Civil Engeering - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Civil Engeering 495991 Townsville Academic Full time Closing on: Nov 15 2026 Position Description Shape the future of sustainable infrastructure through industry-connected teaching and research. Build your academic career with opportunities for research funding, HDR supervision and industry collaboration. Based in Townsville where you can enjoy a tropical lifestyle, with affordable living and the Great Barrier Reef on your doorstep. Full time (36.25 hours per week) | Continuing Appointment Academic Level B - $112,810 - $133,110 Academic Level C - $137,166 - $157,465 Plus 17% super and excellent benefits incl. 5 weeks annual leave, leave loading and flexible work arrangements Shape the future of sustainable infrastructure in the tropics At James Cook University (JCU), our location drives our purpose. Positioned in the heart of Northern Australia, we tackle some of the world's most pressing environmental, infrastructure and sustainability challenges. We're seeking a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Civil Engineering to help shape the next generation of engineers and deliver research that creates real impact across tropical and regional communities. This is a unique opportunity to join a growing Civil Engineering discipline and build your academic career in a region where your expertise can directly influence industry, government and community outcomes. About the Opportunity As a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer, you will strengthen JCU's teaching, research and industry engagement in Civil Engineering, with expertise in Geotechnical Engineering and/or related disciplines. You will contribute to a sustainable future through high-quality teaching, impactful research and meaningful collaboration with industry and government partners. You'll have the opportunity to: Deliver engaging undergraduate and postgraduate teaching in Civil Engineering and related disciplines. Develop and lead a research program addressing challenges relevant to Northern Australia and the tropics. Secure research and consulting income through industry, government and competitive funding opportunities. Supervise Honours, Masters and Higher Degree Research students. Collaborate with industry partners across sectors including mining, critical minerals, sustainable infrastructure and emerging technologies. Raise the profile and impact of JCU's Civil Engineering discipline through research excellence, partnerships and community engagement. About You You are an emerging or established academic who is passionate about engineering education and creating research impact. You will bring: A PhD in Civil Engineering or a closely related discipline. Expertise in Geotechnical Engineering or related areas such as soil mechanics, rock mechanics, mining or sustainable infrastructure. A proven or emerging research profile, demonstrated through publications and research activity. Experience, or strong potential, to attract research funding and build industry partnerships. A commitment to high-quality teaching and student success. The ability to work collaboratively across disciplines and engage effectively with industry, government and community stakeholders. Why JCU? At JCU, your work matters. You'll be part of a university internationally recognised for its focus on the tropics and commitment to creating positive change through education and research. We offer: A supportive and collaborative academic environment. Opportunities to build industry-connected research programs. Access to world-class research facilities and partnerships. Generous leave provisions and flexible work practices. A vibrant tropical lifestyle in Townsville, with easy access to the Great Barrier Reef, rainforests and outdoor adventures. Why Townsville? Enjoy the best of career and lifestyle in Townsville. As Northern Australia's largest city, Townsville offers a thriving engineering sector, affordable living, a vibrant coastal community, and more than 300 days of sunshine each year. With the Great Barrier Reef, Magnetic Island and tropical rainforests on your doorstep, it's the perfect place to build an impactful career while enjoying an exceptional work-life balance. Ready to Make an Impact? If you're excited by the opportunity to influence the future of Civil Engineering education and research while contributing to sustainable outcomes for Northern Australia and the tropical world, we'd love to hear from you. Click the ‘apply’ button where you will be asked to complete an application form or alternatively, please apply directly via the via the JCU careers page and follow the below steps: Complete the application form Upload your current resume Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Mahmood Sadat Noori (07) 4781 5769 or via email Mahmood.SadatNoori@jcu.edu.au Apply now and help build resilient infrastructure and communities for the future. Recommended for you Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Environmental Hydrology Cairns Academic Advance solutions to some of the Tropics’ most pressing land and water challenges. Join James Cook University as a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Environmental Hydrology and build impactful research, inspire future environmental scientists, and collaborate with industry, government and community partners to create real-world environmental outcomes. Scheduling Services Officer Townsville Professional Bring your organizational, problem-solving and communication skills to a fast-paced environment, delivering accurate and efficient timetabling, class registration and scheduling services that support staff, students and the broader University community. Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services, AITHM Cairns Professional Join one of Australia's leading tropical research institutes and lead laboratory and technical services while overseeing the specialised research infrastructure that underpins globally significant health research. Influence strategy, build capability and drive excellence across a diverse and evolving research environment. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/manager-laboratory-and-technical-services-operations-and-safety-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services (Operations and Safety)",
      "description": "Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services (Operations and Safety) - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services (Operations and Safety) 496029 Townsville Professional Technical Full time Closing on: Nov 1 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Are you an experienced leader with a strong background in research laboratory operations or technical service environments? This is an opportunity to lead safe, compliant and high-quality laboratory and technical services that directly support safety, research and service outcomes across JCU. We are seeking a dynamic and experienced Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services (Operations and Safety) to provide strategic and operational leadership across multidisciplinary facilities, teams and services. Laboratory and Technical Services, Education Division Full-time, continuing | 36.25 hours per week Successful candidate must be based in Townsville or willing to relocate before commencement Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, gateway to the Great Barrier Reef and tropical North Queensland HEWL 8: $111,960 - $128,567 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE As Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services (Operations and Safety) , you will lead the planning, prioritisation and delivery of technical and operational services across Academy research facilities and JCU Stores. You will ensure facilities, specialised equipment and resources are safe, compliant and operationally ready, ensuring service delivery to researchers, and embedding effective safety, risk management and compliance practices within the team’s day-to-day operations. With a portfolio spanning varied research disciplines, including an array of biological sciences, chemistry, geology, dentistry and engineering laboratories across multiple facilities and campuses, you will optimise people and resources to support high-quality research, safety and service outcomes. The role also contributes to the broader leadership of Laboratory and Technical Services by building a high-performing and collaborative workplace culture, strengthening cross-team planning and driving service consistency, innovation and continuous improvement. You will lead and develop staff capability, manage workload and performance, and provide high-level technical and operational advice on the feasibility, safety, compliance and resource implications of planned activities. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will bring relevant qualifications, together with demonstrated leadership and operational management experience in a complex laboratory or technical service environment. You will have experience overseeing specialist facilities, technical equipment, analytical instruments and resources, ensuring their safe, effective and compliant operation. Your strong understanding of Workplace Health and Safety legislation will be supported by practical experience in risk management, incident response, compliance monitoring and continuous improvement. You will also demonstrate high-level communication, interpersonal and influencing skills, a proven ability to develop staff and team capability, and the capacity to contribute to strategic initiatives, service innovation and operational improvement. Selection Criteria In addition to the Key Requirements for Success outlined in the Role Profile, the successful applicant must have: Management experience within scientific and/or engineering research laboratories, or comparable technical service environment, with a demonstrated understanding of the operational requirements of complex and regulated laboratory environments. Leadership experience in complex technical operational environments, with evidence of leading diverse teams, strengthening capability and collaboration, and fostering a culture of safety, accountability, innovation and high performance. Experience in the effective operation of biological, chemical and/or engineering laboratories, including physical containment facilities, specialised equipment and analytical instruments, and associated technical services, enabling effective research and service outcomes across broad discipline areas. Demonstrated experience leading safety and compliance within complex laboratory and research environments, with comprehensive knowledge of applicable WHS requirements, risk management, dangerous goods, Scheduled Medicines and Poisons, Australian Laboratory Standards, and Biosecurity, Gene Technology and Radiation regulatory compliance. Demonstrated experience overseeing stores, inventory and/or services within a research or technical environment, ensuring effective resource availability, stock management and responsive service delivery to meet organisational needs. Experience managing complex service demands across multiple disciplines and locations, with demonstrated ability to effectively plan, prioritise and coordinate human, financial and physical resources to meet competing operational and service requirements. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity, Excellence, Integrity and Respect, we support and empower our people through the provisions of: A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville campus HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the 'apply' button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the (1) Key Requirements for Success as outlined in the Role Profile and (2) the Selection Criteria listed in this advertisement, describing how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For enquiries about the role, please contact Dr Amanda Norton at amanda.norton1@jcu.edu.au . ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 616db042 Last Name (required) d6d75984 Email (required) f6e43645 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Environmental Hydrology Cairns Academic Advance solutions to some of the Tropics’ most pressing land and water challenges. Join James Cook University as a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Environmental Hydrology and build impactful research, inspire future environmental scientists, and collaborate with industry, government and community partners to create real-world environmental outcomes. Scheduling Services Officer Townsville Professional Bring your organizational, problem-solving and communication skills to a fast-paced environment, delivering accurate and efficient timetabling, class registration and scheduling services that support staff, students and the broader University community. Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services, AITHM Cairns Professional Join one of Australia's leading tropical research institutes and lead laboratory and technical services while overseeing the specialised research infrastructure that underpins globally significant health research. Influence strategy, build capability and drive excellence across a diverse and evolving research environment. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) 217dfff6 Last Name (required) 4b04fa76 Email (required) f7aadf3d Job Alert e7a9726b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Academic Services Academic Services Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
